essionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42ccd8cf001Cjjx0uSVOg7ZN8\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42ccc8a6001SnxeO1ajlQErwZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774942214370,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42ccd8d2002Zipbe9iNbJp42E\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42ccc8a6001SnxeO1ajlQErwZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_function_76u7h35i5lma_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\projects\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\d361e40f-dc4c-4403-9de6-60b08c54bb83\\\\_default\\\\linkedin-post-day1.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\projects\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\d361e40f-dc4c-4403-9de6-60b08c54bb83\\\\_default\\\\linkedin-post-day1.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: # LinkedIn Post - Day 1\\n2: \\n3: ## Post Draft\\n4: \\n5: ---\\n6: \\n7: **I learned Angular before there was a \\\"Senior\\\" title for it.**\\n8: \\n9: 7 years ago, I started coding from my bedroom. No CS degree. No bootcamp. No mentor.\\n10: \\n11: Just a laptop, free tutorials, and stubbornness.\\n12: \\n13: Today? I'm a Senior Dev working with Angular and .NET daily.\\n14: \\n15: Here's what nobody told me:\\n16: \\n17: 1. **\\\"Self-taught\\\" is not a limitation. It's an advantage.**\\n18:    I learned how to learn. That's a skill most CS grads never develop.\\n19: \\n20: 2. **The first year is the hardest.**\\n21:    I wrote code that makes me cringe today. But I wrote code. Every. Single. Day.\\n22: \\n23: 3. **Degrees don't make developers. Projects do.**\\n24:    My first \\\"real\\\" job came from a portfolio of side projects, not my resume.\\n25: \\n26: If you're where I was 7 years ago - uncertain, self-doubting, wondering if you \\\"belong\\\" in tech:\\n27: \\n28: You belong.\\n29: \\n30: The only thing that separates senior devs from junior devs is time + practice. That's it.\\n31: \\n32: What was your \\\"day 1\\\" moment in tech? 👇\\n33: \\n34: ---\\n35: \\n36: _#SoftwareDeveloper #SelfTaught #Angular #NET #CareerJourney #TechCareers_\\n\\n(End of file - total 36 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"# LinkedIn Post - Day 1\\n\\n## Post Draft\\n\\n---\\n\\n**I learned Angular before there was a \\\"Senior\\\" title for it.**\\n\\n7 years ago, I started coding from my bedroom. No CS degree. No bootcamp. No mentor.\\n\\nJust a laptop, free tutorials, and stubbornness.\\n\\nToday? I'm a Senior Dev working with Angular and .NET daily.\\n\\nHere's what nobody told me:\\n\\n1. **\\\"Self-taught\\\" is not a limitation. It's an advantage.**\\n   I learned how to learn. That's a skill most CS grads never develop.\\n\\n2. **The first year is the hardest.**\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\projects\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\d361e40f-dc4c-4403-9de6-60b08c54bb83\\\\_default\\\\linkedin-post-day1.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774942214355,\"end\":1774942214369}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774942214394,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42ccd8d4001nvaWOu6MIRpFEw\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42ccc8a6001SnxeO1ajlQErwZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_function_76u7h35i5lma_2\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\projects\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\d361e40f-dc4c-4403-9de6-60b08c54bb83\\\\_default\\\\plan.json\"},\"output\":\"<path>C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\projects\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\d361e40f-dc4c-4403-9de6-60b08c54bb83\\\\_default\\\\plan.json</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: {\\n2:   \\\"title\\\": \\\"Brand Strategy & Content Plan\\\",\\n3:   \\\"format\\\": \\\"markdown\\\",\\n4:   \\\"body\\\": \\\"# Self-Taught Labs - Brand Strategy & 30-Day Content Plan\\\\n\\\\n## Company Mission\\\\n**Self-Taught Labs** is a personal brand studio for a self-taught Senior Developer with 7+ years of experience in Angular/.NET who builds open-source AI tools.\\\\n\\\\n## Strategic Goals (Next 90 Days)\\\\n\\\\n### Goal 1: LinkedIn Growth\\\\n- Target: 500+ followers in 90 days\\\\n- Strategy: Position as expert Angular/.NET developer who self-taught AI/ML\\\\n- Content mix: 60% technical, 30% personal brand, 10% industry commentary\\\\n\\\\n### Goal 2: Open-Source AI Tool v1\\\\n- Target: Ship first open-source AI tool\\\\n- Tech stack: Angular + .NET + AI integration\\\\n- Focus: Solve a real problem for Angular/.NET developers\\\\n\\\\n### Goal 3: Content Production\\\\n- Target: 3-4 LinkedIn posts/week\\\\n- Format mix: Carousels, single images, short-form video, threads\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## First Open-Source AI Tool Recommendation\\\\n\\\\n**Recommended: Angular AI Component Generator**\\\\n- Uses AI to generate Angular components from descriptions\\\\n- Solves real pain point: developers spend hours creating boilerplate\\\\n- Leverages existing expertise: Angular + AI = unique positioning\\\\n- Differentiation: Most AI code generators focus on React; Angular is underserved\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 30-Day Content Calendar\\\\n\\\\n### Week 1: Foundation & Credibility (Days 1-7)\\\\n\\\\n| Day | Topic | Format |\\\\n|-----|-------|--------|\\\\n| 1 | I self-taught AI after 7 years of Angular/.NET - My journey | Single post + thread |\\\\n| 2 | Tech tip: Angular signals deep dive | Carousel |\\\\n| 3 | Personal: Why I decided to go self-taught | Single post |\\\\n| 4 | Industry take: Angular vs React in 2026 | Single post |\\\\n| 5 | Open source announcement: My first AI tool coming | Single post |\\\\n| 6 | Buffer/Engagement day | - |\\\\n| 7 | Week recap + engagement | Single post |\\\\n\\\\n### Week 2: Technical Authority (Days 8-14)\\\\n\\\\n| Day | Topic | Format |\\\\n|-----|-------|--------|\\\\n| 8 | .NET + AI integration tutorial preview | Carousel |\\\\n| 9 | The one skill that changed my career | Sing... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n5:   \\\"baseRevisionId\\\": null\\n6: }\\n\\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"{\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Brand Strategy & Content Plan\\\",\\n  \\\"format\\\": \\\"markdown\\\",\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"# Self-Taught Labs - Brand Strategy & 30-Day Content Plan\\\\n\\\\n## Company Mission\\\\n**Self-Taught Labs** is a personal brand studio for a self-taught Senior Developer with 7+ years of experience in Angular/.NET who builds open-source AI tools.\\\\n\\\\n## Strategic Goals (Next 90 Days)\\\\n\\\\n### Goal 1: LinkedIn Growth\\\\n- Target: 500+ followers in 90 days\\\\n- Strategy: Position as expert Angular/.NET developer who self-taught AI/ML\\\\n- Content mix: 60% technical, 30% personal brand, 10% industry commentary\\\\n\\\\n### Goal 2: Open-Source AI Tool v1\\\\n- Target: Ship first open-source AI tool\\\\n- Tech stack: Angular + .NET + AI integration\\\\n- Focus: Solve a real problem for Angular/.NET developers\\\\n\\\\n### Goal 3: Content Production\\\\n- Target: 3-4 LinkedIn posts/week\\\\n- Format mix: Carousels, single images, short-form video, threads\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## First Open-Source AI Tool Recommendation\\\\n\\\\n**Recommended: Angular AI Component Generator**\\\\n- Uses AI to generate Angular components from descriptions\\\\n- Solves real pain point: developers spend hours creating boilerplate\\\\n- Leverages existing expertise: Angular + AI = unique positioning\\\\n- Differentiation: Most AI code generators focus on React; Angular is underserved\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 30-Day Content Calendar\\\\n\\\\n### Week 1: Foundation & Credibility (Days 1-7)\\\\n\\\\n| Day | Topic | Format |\\\\n|-----|-------|--------|\\\\n| 1 | I self-taught AI after 7 years of Angular/.NET - My journey | Single post + thread |\\\\n| 2 | Tech tip: Angular signals deep dive | Carousel |\\\\n| 3 | Personal: Why I decided to go self-taught | Single post |\\\\n| 4 | Industry take: Angular vs React in 2026 | Single post |\\\\n| 5 | Open source announcement: My first AI tool coming | Single post |\\\\n| 6 | Buffer/Engagement day | - |\\\\n| 7 | Week recap + engagement | Single post |\\\\n\\\\n### Week 2: Technical Authority (Days 8-14)\\\\n\\\\n| Day | Topic | Format |\\\\n|-----|-------|--------|\\\\n| 8 | .NET + AI integration tutorial preview | Carousel |\\\\n| 9 | The one skill that changed my career | Sing... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n  \\\"baseRevisionId\\\": null\\n}\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\projects\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\d361e40f-dc4c-4403-9de6-60b08c54bb83\\\\_default\\\\plan.json\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774942214357,\"end\":1774942214393}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774942214493,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42ccd95800177IS29uluYTrYO\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42ccc8a6001SnxeO1ajlQErwZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":30025,\"input\":207,\"output\":218,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":29600}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774942219812,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42ccee1d001KcwksQoZG74YqE\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42ccd95d001rVOIIsfEVdy1Oo\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774942219849,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42ccee23001B2oKrKCjOANdKk\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42ccd95d001rVOIIsfEVdy1Oo\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"glob\",\"callID\":\"call_function_arfo1bq9zrca_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"**/*\"},\"output\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\projects\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\d361e40f-dc4c-4403-9de6-60b08c54bb83\\\\_default\\\\linkedin-post-day1.md\\nC:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\projects\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\d361e40f-dc4c-4403-9de6-60b08c54bb83\\\\_default\\\\plan.json\",\"metadata\":{\"count\":2,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\projects\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\d361e40f-dc4c-4403-9de6-60b08c54bb83\\\\_default\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774942219811,\"end\":1774942219848}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774942219961,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42cceeb5001JynBWPNYf19xBI\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42ccd95d001rVOIIsfEVdy1Oo\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":31465,\"input\":1341,\"output\":332,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":29792}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774942224220,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42ccff580013MUi8uwPXRMj2u\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42cceeb9001DeN82qius9yHPe\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1774942224220,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42ccff5a002eepYk50WVCYc64\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42cceeb9001DeN82qius9yHPe\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\\n\\nI don't have Paperclip environment variables available in this session to connect to the Paperclip API. However, I can see the workspace contains:\\n\\n1. **linkedin-post-day1.md** - A drafted LinkedIn post about your self-taught journey (7 years → Senior Dev with Angular/.NET)\\n2. **plan.json** - Brand strategy for \\\"Self-Taught Labs\\\" with 30-day content calendar\\n\\n**Current post status**: Day 1 post is drafted and ready.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Options:**\\n\\n1. **If you want to connect to Paperclip**: Ensure the session has `PAPERCLIP_API_KEY`, `PAPERCLIP_API_URL`, `PAPERCLIP_AGENT_ID`, and `PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID` environment variables set\\n2. **If you want me to continue with content work**: I can review, refine, or create additional content based on the 30-day plan in `plan.json`\\n\\nWhat would you like me to do?\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774942224219,\"end\":1774942224219}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774942224368,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d42ccffed001AsnYA34dgO23pk\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d42cceeb9001DeN82qius9yHPe\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":31700,\"input\":209,\"output\":387,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":31104}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n"}$paperclip$, NULL, $paperclip$ses_2bd33aa09ffeNZNpM8y0BK8P3h$paperclip$, $paperclip$local_file$paperclip$, $paperclip$c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\743ca119-66ce-4864-99e9-409807dea919\dfde356e-be63-4b62-b1b2-1c75123b34d2.ndjson$paperclip$, $paperclip$53308$paperclip$, $paperclip$33e1c189479940fe01ed93d65592ab90ed8f7f4d303aa47379aa1cf9f66d6b7a$paperclip$, false, $paperclip$e]\",\r\n  \"baseRevisionId\": null\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf `plan` already exists, fetch the current document first and send its latest `baseRevisionId` when you update it.\r\n\r\n## Setting Agent Instructions Path\r\n\r\nUse the dedicated route instead of generic `PATCH /api/agents/:id` when you need to set an agent's instructions markdown path (for example `AGENTS.md`).\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nPATCH /api/agents/{agentId}/instructions-path\r\n{\r\n  \"path\": \"agents/cmo/AGENTS.md\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nRules:\r\n\r\n- Allowed for: the target agent itself, or an ancestor manager in that agent's reporting chain.\r\n- For `codex_local` and `claude_local`, default config key is `instructionsFilePath`.\r\n- Relative paths are resolved against the target agent's `adapterConfig.cwd`; absolute paths are accepted as-is.\r\n- To clear the path, send `{ \"path\": null }`.\r\n- For adapters with a different key, provide it explicitly:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nPATCH /api/agents/{agentId}/instructions-path\r\n{\r\n  \"path\": \"/absolute/path/to/AGENTS.md\",\r\n  \"adapterConfigKey\": \"yourAdapterSpecificPathField\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Key Endpoints (Quick Reference)\r\n\r\n| Action                                    | Endpoint                                                                                   |\r\n| ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\r\n| My identity                               | `GET /api/agents/me`                                                                       |\r\n| My compact inbox                          | `GET /api/agents/me/inbox-lite`                                                            |\r\n| My assignments                            | `GET /api/companies/:companyId/issues?assigneeAgentId=:id&status=todo,in_progress,blocked` |\r\n| Checkout task                             | `POST /api/issues/:issueId/checkout`                                                       |\r\n| Get task + ancestors                      | `GET /api/issues/:issueId`                                                                 |\r\n| List issue documents                      | `GET /api/issues/:issueId/documents`                                                       |\r\n| Get issue document                        | `GET /api/issues/:issueId/documents/:key`                                                  |\r\n| Create/update issue document              | `PUT /api/issues/:issueId/documents/:key`                                                  |\r\n| Get issue document revisions              | `GET /api/issues/:issueId/documents/:key/revisions`                                        |\r\n| Get compact heartbeat context             | `GET /api/issues/:issueId/heartbeat-context`                                               |\r\n| Get comments                              | `GET /api/issues/:issueId/comments`                                                        |\r\n| Get comment delta                         | `GET /api/issues/:issueId/comments?after=:commentId&order=asc`                             |\r\n| Get specific comment                      | `GET /api/issues/:issueId/comments/:commentId`                                             |\r\n| Update task                               | `PATCH /api/issues/:issueId` (optional `comment` field)                                    |\r\n| Add comment                               | `POST /api/issues/:issueId/comments`                                                       |\r\n| Create subtask                            | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/issues`                                                    |\r\n| Generate OpenClaw invite prompt (CEO)     | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/openclaw/invite-prompt`                                    |\r\n| Create project                            | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/projects`                                                  |\r\n| Create project workspace                  | `POST /api/projects/:projectId/workspaces`                                                 |\r\n| Set instructions path                     | `PATCH /api/agents/:agentId/instructions-path`                                             |\r\n| Release task                              | `POST /api/issues/:issueId/release`                                                        |\r\n| List agents                               | `GET /api/companies/:companyId/agents`                                                     |\r\n| List company skills                       | `GET /api/companies/:companyId/skills`                                                     |\r\n| Import company skills                     | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/skills/import`                                             |\r\n| Scan project workspaces for skills        | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/skills/scan-projects`                                      |\r\n| Sync agent desired skills                 | `POST /api/agents/:agentId/skills/sync`                                                    |\r\n| Preview CEO-safe company import          | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/imports/preview`                                           |\r\n| Apply CEO-safe company import            | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/imports/apply`                                             |\r\n| Preview company export                   | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/exports/preview`                                           |\r\n| Build company export                     | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/exports`                                                   |\r\n| Dashboard                                 | `GET /api/companies/:companyId/dashboard`                                                  |\r\n| Search issues                             | `GET /api/companies/:companyId/issues?q=search+term`                                       |\r\n| Upload attachment (multipart, field=file) | `POST /api/companies/:companyId/issues/:issueId/attachments`                               |\r\n| List issue attachments                    | `GET /api/issues/:issueId/attachments`                                                     |\r\n| Get attachment content                    | `GET /api/attachments/:attachmentId/content`                                               |\r\n| Delete attachment                         | `DELETE /api/attachments/:attachmentId`                                                    |\r\n\r\n## Company Import / Export\r\n\r\nUse the company-scoped routes when a CEO agent needs to inspect or move package content.\r\n\r\n- CEO-safe imports:\r\n  - `POST /api/companies/{companyId}/imports/preview`\r\n  - `POST /api/companies/{companyId}/imports/apply`\r\n- Allowed callers: board users and the CEO agent of that same company.\r\n- Safe import rules:\r\n  - existing-company imports are non-destructive\r\n  - `replace` is rejected\r\n  - collisions resolve with `rename` or `skip`\r\n  - issues are always created as new issues\r\n- CEO agents may use the safe routes with `target.mode = \"new_company\"` to create a new company directly. Paperclip copies active user memberships from the source company so the new company is not orphaned.\r\n\r\nFor export, preview first and keep tasks explicit:\r\n\r\n- `POST /api/companies/{companyId}/exports/preview`\r\n- `POST /api/companies/{companyId}/exports`\r\n- Export preview defaults to `issues: false`\r\n- Add `issues` or `projectIssues` only when you intentionally need task files\r\n- Use `selectedFiles` to narrow the final package to specific agents, skills, projects, or tasks after you inspect the preview inventory\r\n\r\n## Searching Issues\r\n\r\nUse the `q` query parameter on the issues list endpoint to search across titles, identifiers, descriptions, and comments:\r\n\r\n```\r\nGET /api/companies/{companyId}/issues?q=dockerfile\r\n```\r\n\r\nResults are ranked by relevance: title matches first, then identifier, description, and comments. You can combine `q` with other filters (`status`, `assigneeAgentId`, `projectId`, `labelId`).\r\n\r\n## Self-Test Playbook (App-Level)\r\n\r\nUse this when validating Paperclip itself (assignment flow, checkouts, run visibility, and status transitions).\r\n\r\n1. Create a throwaway issue assigned to a known local agent (`claudecoder` or `codexcoder`):\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nnpx paperclipai issue create \\\r\n  --company-id \"$PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID\" \\\r\n  --title \"Self-test: assignment/watch flow\" \\\r\n  --description \"Temporary validation issue\" \\\r\n  --status todo \\\r\n  --assignee-agent-id \"$PAPERCLIP_AGENT_ID\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. Trigger and watch a heartbeat for that assignee:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nnpx paperclipai heartbeat run --agent-id \"$PAPERCLIP_AGENT_ID\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n3. Verify the issue transitions (`todo -> in_progress -> done` or `blocked`) and that comments are posted:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nnpx paperclipai issue get <issue-id-or-identifier>\r\n```\r\n\r\n4. Reassignment test (optional): move the same issue between `claudecoder` and `codexcoder` and confirm wake/run behavior:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nnpx paperclipai issue update <issue-id> --assignee-agent-id <other-agent-id> --status todo\r\n```\r\n\r\n5. Cleanup: mark temporary issues done/cancelled with a clear note.\r\n\r\nIf you use direct `curl` during these tests, include `X-Paperclip-Run-Id` on all mutating issue requests whenever running inside a heartbeat.\r\n\r\n## Full Reference\r\n\r\nFor detailed API tables, JSON response schemas, worked examples (IC and Manager heartbeats), governance/approvals, cross-team delegation rules, error codes, issue lifecycle diagram, and the common mistakes table, read: `skills/paperclip/references/api-reference.md`\n\nBase directory for this skill: file:///C:/Users/THANHSANG/.claude/skills/paperclip\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n<file>C:\\Users\\THANHSANG\\.claude\\skills\\paperclip\\references\\company-skills.md</file>\n<file>C:\\Users\\THANHSANG\\.claude\\skills\\paperclip\\references\\api-reference.md</file>\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"paperclip","dir":"C:\\Users\\THANHSANG\\.claude\\skills\\paperclip","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: paperclip","time":{"start":1774942187427,"end":1774942187487}}}}
