\\\\linkedin-post-day1.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: # LinkedIn Post - Day 1\\n2: \\n3: ## Post Draft\\n4: \\n5: ---\\n6: \\n7: **I learned Angular before there was a \\\"Senior\\\" title for it.**\\n8: \\n9: 7 years ago, I started coding from my bedroom. No CS degree. No bootcamp. No mentor.\\n10: \\n11: Just a laptop, free tutorials, and stubbornness.\\n12: \\n13: Today? I'm a Senior Dev working with Angular and .NET daily.\\n14: \\n15: Here's what nobody told me:\\n16: \\n17: 1. **\\\"Self-taught\\\" is not a limitation. It's an advantage.**\\n18:    I learned how to learn. That's a skill most CS grads never develop.\\n19: \\n20: 2. **The first year is the hardest.**\\n21:    I wrote code that makes me cringe today. But I wrote code. Every. Single. Day.\\n22: \\n23: 3. **Degrees don't make developers. Projects do.**\\n24:    My first \\\"real\\\" job came from a portfolio of side projects, not my resume.\\n25: \\n26: If you're where I was 7 years ago - uncertain, self-doubting, wondering if you \\\"belong\\\" in tech:\\n27: \\n28: You belong.\\n29: \\n30: The only thing that separates senior devs from junior devs is time + practice. That's it.\\n31: \\n32: What was your \\\"day 1\\\" moment in tech? 👇\\n33: \\n34: ---\\n35: \\n36: _#SoftwareDeveloper #SelfTaught #Angular #NET #CareerJourney #TechCareers_\\n\\n(End of file - total 36 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"# LinkedIn Post - Day 1\\n\\n## Post Draft\\n\\n---\\n\\n**I learned Angular before there was a \\\"Senior\\\" title for it.**\\n\\n7 years ago, I started coding from my bedroom. No CS degree. No bootcamp. No mentor.\\n\\nJust a laptop, free tutorials, and stubbornness.\\n\\nToday? I'm a Senior Dev working with Angular and .NET daily.\\n\\nHere's what nobody told me:\\n\\n1. **\\\"Self-taught\\\" is not a limitation. It's an advantage.**\\n   I learned how to learn. That's a skill most CS grads never develop.\\n\\n2. **The first year is the hardest.**\",\"truncated\":fals