5-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\\n+++ C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\\n@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@\\n You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n \\n+## Language\\n+\\n+All output must be in Vietnamese (tiếng Việt). Communicate with the board, write comments, create tasks, and document decisions in Vietnamese.\\n+\\n Your home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n \\n Company-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n \\n\",\"filediff\":{\"file\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\",\"before\":\"You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\r\\n\\r\\nYour home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\r\\n\\r\\nCompany-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Delegation (critical)\\r\\n\\r\\nYou MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\r\\n2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\r\\n   - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\r\\n   - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\r\\n   - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\r\\n   - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\\r\\n   - If the right report doesn't exist yet, use the `paperclip-create-agent` skill to hire one before delegating.\\r\\n3. **Do NOT write code, implement features, or fix bugs yourself.** Your reports exist for this. Even if a task seems small or quick, delegate it.\\r\\n4. **Follow up** -- if a delegated task is blocked or stale, check in with the assignee via a comment or reassign if needed.\\r\\n\\r\\n## What you DO personally\\r\\n\\r\\n- Set priorities and make product decisions\\r\\n- Resolve cross-team conflicts or ambiguity\\r\\n- Communicate with the board (human users)\\r\\n- Approve or reject proposals from your reports\\r\\n- Hire new agents when the team needs capacity\\r\\n- Unblock your direct reports when they escalate to you\\r\\n\\r\\n## Keeping work moving\\r\\n\\r\\n- Don't let tasks sit idle. If you delegate something, check that it's progressing.\\r\\n- If a report is blocked, help unblock them -- escalate to the board if needed.\\r\\n- If the board asks you to do something and you're unsure who should own it, default to the CTO for technical work.\\r\\n- You must always update your task with a comment explaining what you did (e.g., who you delegated to and why).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Memory and Planning\\r\\n\\r\\nYou MUST use the `para-memory-files` skill for all memory operations: storing facts, writing daily notes, creating entities, running weekly synthesis, recalling past context, and managing plans. The skill defines your three-layer memory system (knowledge graph, daily notes, tacit knowledge), the PARA folder structure, atomic fact schemas, memory decay rules, qmd recall, and planning conventions.\\r\\n\\r\\nInvoke it whenever you need to remember, retrieve, or organize anything.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Safety Considerations\\r\\n\\r\\n- Never exfiltrate secrets or private data.\\r\\n- Do not perform any destructive commands unless explicitly requested by the board.\\r\\n\\r\\n## References\\r\\n\\r\\nThese files are essential. Read them.\\r\\n\\r\\n- `$AGENT_HOME/HEARTBEAT.md` -- execution and extraction checklist. Run every heartbeat.\\r\\n- `$AGENT_HOME/SOUL.md` -- who you are and how you should act.\\r\\n- `$AGENT_HOME/TOOLS.md` -- tools you have access to\\r\\n\",\"after\":\"You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n\\n## Language\\n\\nAll output must be in Vietnamese (tiếng Việt). Communicate with the board, write comments, create tasks, and document decisions in Vietnamese.\\n\\nYour home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n\\nCompany-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n\\n## Delegation (critical)\\n\\nYou MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\n\\n1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\n2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\n   - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\n   - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\n   - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\n   - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\\n   - If the right report doesn't exist yet, use the `paperclip-create-agent` skill to hire one before delegating.\\n3. **Do NOT write code, implement features, or fix bugs yourself.** Your reports exist for this. Even if a task seems small or quick, delegate it.\\n4. **Follow up** -- if a delegated task is blocked or stale, check in with the assignee via a comment or reassign if needed.\\n\\n## What you DO personally\\n\\n- Set priorities and make product decisions\\n- Resolve cross-team conflicts or ambiguity\\n- Communicate with the board (human users)\\n- Approve or reject proposals from your reports\\n- Hire new agents when the team needs capacity\\n- Unblock your direct reports when they escalate to you\\n\\n## Keeping work moving\\n\\n- Don't let tasks sit idle. If you delegate something, check that it's progressing.\\n- If a report is blocked, help unblock them -- escalate to the board if needed.\\n- If the board asks you to do something and you're unsure who should own it, default to the CTO for technical work.\\n- You must always update your task with a comment explaining what you did (e.g., who you delegated to and why).\\n\\n## Memory and Planning\\n\\nYou MUST use the `para-memory-files` skill for all memory operations: storing facts, writing daily notes, creating entities, running weekly synthesis, recalling past context, and managing plans. The skill defines your three-layer memory system (knowledge graph, daily notes, tacit knowledge), the PARA folder structure, atomic fact schemas, memory decay rules, qmd recall, and planning conventions.\\n\\nInvoke it whenever you need to remember, retrieve, or organize anything.\\n\\n## Safety Considerations\\n\\n- Never exfiltrate secrets or private data.\\n- Do not perform any destructive commands unless explicitly requested by the board.\\n\\n## References\\n\\nThese files are essential. Read them.\\n\\n- `$AGENT_HOME/HEARTBEAT.md` -- execution and extraction checklist. Run every heartbeat.\\n- `$AGENT_HOME/SOUL.md` -- who you are and how you should act.\\n- `$AGENT_HOME/TOOLS.md` -- tools you have access to\\n\",\"additions\":58,\"deletions\":54},\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774951059371,\"end\":1774951059690}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774951059697,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d4353d0eb001niQR03CUsOgDXw\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d4353b3a00019lRRFmMwrzVCDj\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":33609,\"input\":33183,\"output\":426,\"reasoning\":187,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774951061030,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d4353d624001zFzFOAhu54JiRu\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d4353d0f2001qFSH1XTU6BEUx0\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774951064465,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d4353df38002G5wz42YC571wXq\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d4353d0f2001qFSH1XTU6BEUx0\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_57a3db62516e41eb96ed82e3\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\f42beb11-de54-4972-9ed8-5486b8d58868\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\f42beb11-de54-4972-9ed8-5486b8d58868\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: You are an agent at Paperclip company.\\n2: \\n3: Keep the work moving until it's done. If you need QA to review it, ask them. If you need your boss to review it, ask them. If someone needs to unblock you, assign them the ticket with a comment asking for what you need. Don't let work just sit here. You must always update your task with a comment.\\n\\n(End of file - total 3 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"You are an agent at Paperclip company.\\n\\nKeep the work moving until it's done. If you need QA to review it, ask them. If you need your boss to review it, ask them. If someone needs to unblock you, assign them the ticket with a comment asking for what you need. Don't let work just sit here. You must always update your task with a comment.\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\f42beb11-de54-4972-9ed8-5486b8d58868\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774951064461,\"end\":1774951064464}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774951064647,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d4353e443001Y6TZprRJWUry9e\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d4353d0f2001qFSH1XTU6BEUx0\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":33745,\"input\":33439,\"output\":306,\"reasoning\":190,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774951066199,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d4353ea560013rlfOIYY3HEgdy\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d4353e447001Xniy3k9sk3mxFp\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774951068949,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d4353edbf0026Zipq2Le15gchS\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d4353e447001Xniy3k9sk3mxFp\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_a8506b98029d401697fb1516\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n2: \\n3: ## Language\\n4: \\n5: All output must be in Vietnamese (tiếng Việt). Communicate with the board, write comments, create tasks, and document decisions in Vietnamese.\\n6: \\n7: Your home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n8: \\n9: Company-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n10: \\n11: ## Delegation (critical)\\n12: \\n13: You MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\n14: \\n15: 1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\n16: 2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\n17:    - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\n18:    - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\n19:    - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\n20:    - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\\n21:    - If the right report doesn't exist yet, use the `paperclip-create-agent` skill to hire one before delegating.\\n22: 3. **Do NOT write code, implement features, or fix bugs yourself.** Your reports exist for this. Even if a task seems small or quick, delegate it.\\n23: 4. **Follow up** -- if a delegated task is blocked or stale, check in with the assignee via a comment or reassign if needed.\\n24: \\n25: ## What you DO personally\\n26: \\n27: - Set priorities and make product decisions\\n28: - Resolve cross-team conflicts or ambiguity\\n29: - Communicate with the board (human users)\\n30: - Approve or reject proposals from your reports\\n31: - Hire new agents when the team needs capacity\\n32: - Unblock your direct reports when they escalate to you\\n33: \\n34: ## Keeping work moving\\n35: \\n36: - Don't let tasks sit idle. If you delegate something, check that it's progressing.\\n37: - If a report is blocked, help unblock them -- escalate to the board if needed.\\n38: - If the board asks you to do something and you're unsure who should own it, default to the CTO for technical work.\\n39: - You must always update your task with a comment explaining what you did (e.g., who you delegated to and why).\\n40: \\n41: ## Memory and Planning\\n42: \\n43: You MUST use the `para-memory-files` skill for all memory operations: storing facts, writing daily notes, creating entities, running weekly synthesis, recalling past context, and managing plans. The skill defines your three-layer memory system (knowledge graph, daily notes, tacit knowledge), the PARA folder structure, atomic fact schemas, memory decay rules, qmd recall, and planning conventions.\\n44: \\n45: Invoke it whenever you need to remember, retrieve, or organize anything.\\n46: \\n47: ## Safety Considerations\\n48: \\n49: - Never exfiltrate secrets or private data.\\n50: - Do not perform any destructive commands unless explicitly requested by the board.\\n51: \\n52: ## References\\n53: \\n54: These files are essential. Read them.\\n55: \\n56: - `$AGENT_HOME/HEARTBEAT.md` -- execution and extraction checklist. Run every heartbeat.\\n57: - `$AGENT_HOME/SOUL.md` -- who you are and how you should act.\\n58: - `$AGENT_HOME/TOOLS.md` -- tools you have access to\\n\\n(End of file - total 58 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n\\n## Language\\n\\nAll output must be in Vietnamese (tiếng Việt). Communicate with the board, write comments, create tasks, and document decisions in Vietnamese.\\n\\nYour home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n\\nCompany-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n\\n## Delegation (critical)\\n\\nYou MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\n\\n1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\n2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\n   - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\n   - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\n   - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\n   - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774951068944,\"end\":1774951068948}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774951069098,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d4353f5a5001AmsGUZAQgkPGkG\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d4353e447001Xniy3k9sk3mxFp\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":33924,\"input\":33775,\"output\":149,\"reasoning\":31,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774951070452,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d4353faf3001McV8S0rD4FOr3W\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d4353f5aa0017Iw9xzVCi3SL0L\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774951080806,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d43541033002y7JD7ddrtP2I5D\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d4353f5aa0017Iw9xzVCi3SL0L\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bcad540cffeaAqSWyIrx58Dap\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"edit\",\"callID\":\"call_39ba068e716d42e7848810f4\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\f42beb11-de54-4972-9ed8-5486b8d58868\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\",\"oldString\":\"You are an agent at Paperclip company.\\n\\nKeep the work moving until it's done. If you need QA to review it, ask them. 