md\",\"metadata\":{\"count\":10,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774953831126,\"end\":1774953831127}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774953831323,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e1ad70022Pf3zCVAn7Uy2l\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"1e778bb0f71da09ca6129300b75af9f3488ca11b\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d437dfb66001up1UpoYS81UOo8\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":44049,\"input\":112,\"output\":609,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":43328}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774953840999,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e415a001Zl2b9K9i3aFv0g\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d437e1c56001wKBYQcvHc1rb1V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"snapshot\":\"1e778bb0f71da09ca6129300b75af9f3488ca11b\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774953841001,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e415f001IOxXscRha5KRwb\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d437e1c56001wKBYQcvHc1rb1V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_function_xnutm37hum2m_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\plans\\\\content-operations-plan-2026-04.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\plans\\\\content-operations-plan-2026-04.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: # Content Operations Plan — AI Thuc Dong Lab\\n2: \\n3: # Created: 2026-03-31\\n4: \\n5: # Owner: CEO\\n6: \\n7: # Supersedes: None\\n8: \\n9: # Status: Active\\n10: \\n11: ---\\n12: \\n13: ## Company Mission\\n14: \\n15: Build personal brand \\\"AI Thuc Dong Lab\\\" — leading niche of AI Productivity & Automation in Vietnam.\\n16: \\n17: **Targets (6 months):**\\n18: \\n19: - 50,000 followers across all channels\\n20: - $2,000/month revenue from SaaS Affiliate\\n21: - Simplify AI knowledge for mass audience\\n22: \\n23: **Content Philosophy:**\\n24: \\n25: - Vietnamese language, natural tone\\n26: - Simple enough for grade 7 students to understand\\n27: - Focus on AI productivity tools\\n28: - Actionable, not theoretical\\n29: \\n30: ---\\n31: \\n32: ## 1-Month Content Calendar (Month 1: April 2026)\\n33: \\n34: ### Content Pillars\\n35: \\n36: | Pillar                     | Weight | Description                                           |\\n37: | -------------------------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\\n38: | Tool Reviews               | 30%    | Deep-dive AI tools, pros/cons, pricing                |\\n39: | How-To Guides              | 25%    | Step-by-step tutorials, automation recipes            |\\n40: | Trend Analysis             | 15%    | AI news breakdown, what it means for Vietnamese users |\\n41: | Productivity Tips          | 15%    | Quick wins, workflow hacks                            |\\n42: | Personal/Behind-the-Scenes | 10%    | Journey, lessons, community Q&A                       |\\n43: | Affiliate Promos           | 5%     | Soft-sell tool recommendations with affiliate links   |\\n44: \\n45: ### Weekly Rhythm\\n46: \\n47: | Day       | Content Type                | Channels                    |\\n48: | --------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------- |\\n49: | Monday    | Tool Review (long-form)     | YouTube, LinkedIn, Facebook |\\n50: | Tuesday   | How-To Guide (tutorial)     | YouTube, TikTok, Facebook   |\\n51: | Wednesday | Trend Analysis (commentary) | LinkedIn, Threads, Facebook |\\n52: | Thursday  | Productivity Tip (quick)    | TikTok, Threads, LinkedIn   |\\n53: | Friday    | How-To Guide (tutorial)     | YouTube, TikTok, Facebook   |\\n54: | Saturday  | Personal/BTS (casual)       | Threads, Facebook, TikTok   |\\n55: | Sunday    | Weekly roundup / Q&A        | LinkedIn, Facebook, Threads |\\n56: \\n57: ### Month 1 Content Schedule (28 pieces)\\n58: \\n59: #### Week 1 (Mar 31 - Apr 6): Foundation — \\\"AI Basics Everyone Should Know\\\"\\n60: \\n61: | #   | Title                                                       | Pillar       | Channels        | Format                 |\\n62: | --- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | --------------- | ---------------------- |\\n63: | 1   | \\\"5 AI Tools Free Students Need in 2026\\\"                     | Tool Review  | YT, LI, FB      | Video 8-10min + post   |\\n64: | 2   | \\\"How to Use ChatGPT to Write Essays (Step-by-Step)\\\"         | How-To       | YT, TT, FB      | Video 5-7min + shorts  |\\n65: | 3   | \\\"Google Gemini vs ChatGPT: Which is Better for Vietnamese?\\\" | Trend        | LI, Threads, FB | Text post + thread     |\\n66: | 4   | \\\"3 AI Prompts That Save 2 Hours Daily\\\"                      | Productivity | TT, Threads, LI | Short video + carousel |\\n67: | 5   | \\\"How to Automate Email Responses with AI\\\"                   | How-To       | YT, TT, FB      | Video 6-8min           |\\n68: | 6   | \\\"Why I Started AI Thuc Dong Lab\\\"                            | Personal     | Threads, FB, TT | Text + short video     |\\n69: | 7   | \\\"Week 1 Recap: Best AI Tools We Tested\\\"                     | Roundup      | LI, FB, Threads | Summary post           |\\n70: \\n71: #### Week 2 (Apr 7-13): \\\"AI for Work & Study\\\"\\n72: \\n73: | #   | Title                                              | Pillar       | Channels        | Format            |\\n74: | --- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | --------------- | ----------------- |\\n75: | 8   | \\\"Notion AI Full Review: Worth the Money?\\\"          | Tool Review  | YT, LI, FB      | Video 10-12min    |\\n76: | 9   | \\\"How to Create Presentations with AI in 5 Minutes\\\" | How-To       | YT, TT, FB      | Video 5-7min      |\\n77: | 10  | \\\"OpenAI o3 Released — What It Means for You\\\"       | Trend        | LI, Threads, FB | Analysis post     |\\n78: | 11  | \\\"The 1-Minute Rule: AI + Time Management\\\"          | Productivity | TT, Threads, LI | Short video + tip |\\n79: | 12  | \\\"How to Build a Personal Knowledge Base with AI\\\"   | How-To       | YT, TT, FB      | Video 8-10min     |\\n80: | 13  | \\\"My Biggest Mistake Learning AI (So You Don't)\\\"    | Personal     | Threads, FB, TT | Story post        |\\n81: | 14  | \\\"Week 2 Recap: AI Tools That Actually Work\\\"        | Roundup      | LI, FB, Threads | Summary post      |\\n82: \\n83: #### Week 3 (Apr 14-20): \\\"Automation for Everyone\\\"\\n84: \\n85: | #   | Title                                           | Pillar       | Channels        | Format             |\\n86: | --- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------ | --------------- | ------------------ |\\n87: | 15  | \\\"Zapier vs Make.com: Best Automation Tool 2026\\\" | Tool Review  | YT, LI, FB      | Video 10-12min     |\\n88: | 16  | \\\"How to Auto-Summarize YouTube Videos with AI\\\"  | How-To       | YT, TT, FB      | Video 5-7min       |\\n89: | 17  | \\\"AI Agents Are Here — Should You Care?\\\"         | Trend        | LI, Threads, FB | Opinion piece      |\\n90: | 18  | \\\"5 Chrome Extensions That Make You 10x Faster\\\"  | Productivity | TT, Threads, LI | Short video + list |\\n91: | 19  | \\\"How to Create AI Chatbots for Your Business\\\"   | How-To       | YT, TT, FB      | Video 8-10min      |\\n92: | 20  | \\\"What I Learned from 100 AI Tool Tests\\\"         | Personal     | Threads, FB, TT | Lessons post       |\\n93: | 21  | \\\"Week 3 Recap: Automation Wins\\\"                 | Roundup      | LI, FB, Threads | Summary post       |\\n94: \\n95: #### Week 4 (Apr 21-28): \\\"AI Money — Affiliate & Side Hustles\\\"\\n96: \\n97: | #   | Title                                                | Pillar       | Channels        | Format                     |\\n98: | --- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | --------------- | -------------------------- |\\n99: | 22  | \\\"Top 5 AI Affiliate Programs That Actually Pay\\\"      | Tool Review  | YT, LI, FB      | Video 10-12min + affiliate |\\n100: | 23  | \\\"How I Made My First $100 with AI Affiliate\\\"         | How-To       | YT, TT, FB      | Video 8-10min              |\\n101: | 24  | \\\"Jasper AI vs Copy.ai: Best for Vietnamese Content?\\\" | Trend        | LI, Threads, FB | Comparison post            |\\n102: | 25  | \\\"The $0 AI Stack: Free Tools That Replace Paid Ones\\\" | Productivity | TT, Threads, LI | Short video + list         |\\n103: | 26  | \\\"How to Start an AI YouTube Channel (Full Guide)\\\"    | How-To       | YT, TT, FB      | Video 10-12min             |\\n104: | 27  | \\\"Month 1 Results: What Worked, What Didn't\\\"          | Personal     | Threads, FB, TT | Transparency post          |\\n105: | 28  | \\\"Month 1 Recap + Month 2 Preview\\\"                    | Roundup      | LI, FB, Threads | Summary post               |\\n106: \\n107: ---\\n108: \\n109: ## Channel Strategy\\n110: \\n111: ### LinkedIn\\n112: \\n113: - **Frequency:** 4 posts/week (Mon, Wed, Thu, Sun)\\n114: - **Format:** Long-form text posts, carousels, article links\\n115: - **Tone:** Professional, analytical, thought leadership\\n116: - **Goal:** Build authority, attract B2B audience\\n117: \\n118: ### Threads\\n119: \\n120: - **Frequency:** 5 posts/week (Wed, Thu, Sat, Sun + daily replies)\\n121: - **Format:** Short text threads, quick tips, engagement\\n122: - **Tone:** Conversational, authentic, slightly casual\\n123: - **Goal:** Community building, viral reach\\n124: \\n125: ### TikTok\\n126: \\n127: - **Frequency:** 4 videos/week (Tue, Thu, Fri, Sat)\\n128: - **Format:** 30-60sec vertical videos, screen recordings\\n129: - **Tone:** Energetic, visual, hook-driven\\n130: - **Goal:** Mass reach, younger audience, brand awareness\\n131: \\n132: ### YouTube\\n133: \\n134: - **Frequency:** 3 videos/week (Mon, Tue/Fri alternating, 1 long-form)\\n135: - **Format:** 5-12min tutorials, reviews, deep-dives\\n136: - **Tone:** Educational, structured, value-first\\n137: - **Goal:** Evergreen content, SEO, affiliate revenue\\n138: \\n139: ### Facebook\\n140: \\n141: - **Frequency:** 5 posts/week (Mon, Tue, Wed, Fri, Sun)\\n142: - **Format:** Video posts, image posts, group engagement\\n143: - **Tone:** Friendly, community-oriented, Vietnamese-first\\n144: - **Goal:** Local audience, community building, sharing\\n145: \\n146: ---\\n147: \\n148: ## Hiring Plan\\n149: \\n150: ### Phase 1: Immediate (Week 1-2) — CMO ✅ Submitted for Approval\\n151: \\n152: **CMO — Chief Marketing Officer**\\n153: \\n154: - **Role:** Own content strategy, channel management, brand voice\\n155: - **Responsibilities:**\\n156:   - Execute content calendar\\n157:   - Manage all 5 channels\\n158:   - Maintain brand voice consistency\\n159:   - Report weekly metrics to CEO\\n160: - **Reports to:** CEO\\n161: \\n162: ### Phase 2: Month 1 (Week 2-4) — Core Team\\n163: \\n164: **Market Researcher**\\n165: \\n166: - **Role:** SaaS & AI trend research\\n167: - **Responsibilities:**\\n168:   - Weekly AI tool landscape scan\\n169:   - Competitor content analysis\\n170:   - Affiliate program discovery & evaluation\\n171:   - Trend reports for content team\\n172: - **Reports to:** CMO\\n173: \\n174: **Omnichannel Writer**\\n175: \\n176: - **Role:** Content creation across all platforms\\n177: - **Responsibilities:**\\n178:   - Write LinkedIn posts, Threads, Facebook posts\\n179:   - Script YouTube videos and TikToks\\n180:   - Adapt one piece of content into 5 formats\\n181:   - Maintain Vietnamese natural tone\\n182: - **Reports to:** CMO\\n183: \\n184: ### Phase 3: Month 2 — Growth & Quality\\n185: \\n186: **QA & Affiliate Manager**\\n187: \\n188: - **Role:** Quality control + affiliate revenue optimization\\n189: - **Responsibilities:**\\n190:   - Review all content before publishing\\n191:   - Manage affiliate link placement and tracking\\n192:   - A/B test content formats\\n193:   - Revenue reporting and optimization\\n194: - **Reports to:** CMO\\n195: \\n196: ---\\n197: \\n198: ## Task Breakdown (Ready for Delegation)\\n199: \\n200: ### Content Production Tasks (for CMO team)\\n201: \\n202: | Task ID | Title                             | Assignee     | Priority | Description                                            |\\n203: | ------- | --------------------------------- | ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\\n204: | C-001   | Set up content calendar system    | CMO          | High     | Create tracking system for 28 pieces across 5 channels |\\n205: | C-002   | Produce Week 1 content (7 pieces) | CMO + Writer | Critical | Execute Week 1 content plan                            |\\n206: | C-003   | Produce Week 2 content (7 pieces) | CMO + Writer | High     | Execute Week 2 content plan                            |\\n207: | C-004   | Produce Week 3 content (7 pieces) | CMO + Writer | High     | Execute Week 3 content plan                            |\\n208: | C-005   | Produce Week 4 content (7 pieces) | CMO + Writer | High     | Execute Week 4 content plan                            |\\n209: | C-006   | Set up affiliate accounts         | CMO + QA     | Medium   | Register for top 5 affiliate programs                  |\\n210: | C-007   | Weekly metrics report             | CMO          | Medium   | Track followers, engagement, revenue                   |\\n211: \\n212: ### Research Tasks (for Market Researcher)\\n213: \\n214: | Task ID | Title                        | Assignee   | Priority | Description                                     |\\n215: | ------- | ---------------------------- | ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\\n216: | R-001   | AI tool landscape scan       | Researcher | High     | Weekly report on new AI tools                   |\\n217: | R-002   | Competitor content analysis  | Researcher | Medium   | Analyze top 10 VN AI content creators           |\\n218: | R-003   | Affiliate program evaluation | Researcher | High     | Find and rank best-paying AI affiliate programs |\\n219: \\n220: ### Quality Tasks (for QA Manager)\\n221: \\n222: | Task ID | Title                         | Assignee | Priority | Description                                |\\n223: | ------- | ----------------------------- | -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\\n224: | Q-001   | Content review checklist      | QA       | High     | Create QA checklist for all content        |\\n225: | Q-002   | Affiliate link tracking setup | QA       | Medium   | Implement tracking for all affiliate links |\\n226: | Q-003   | Monthly quality audit         | QA       | Low      | Review all published content for quality   |\\n227: \\n228: ---\\n229: \\n230: ## Success Metrics (Month 1)\\n231: \\n232: | Metric                   | Target | Measurement                  |\\n233: | ------------------------ | ------ | ---------------------------- |\\n234: | Total Followers          | 2,000  | Sum across all 5 channels    |\\n235: | Content Pieces Published | 28     | Per calendar                 |\\n236: | Engagement Rate          | 5%+    | Likes + comments / followers |\\n237: | Affiliate Revenue        | $50    | First month, baseline        |\\n238: | YouTube Views            | 5,000  | Total across all videos      |\\n239: | LinkedIn Impressions     | 20,000 | Total post impressions       |\\n240: \\n241: ---\\n242: \\n243: ## Notes\\n244: \\n245: - All content in Vietnamese\\n246: - Grade 7 readability target\\n247: - No jargon without explanation\\n248: - Affiliate links should feel natural, not salesy\\n249: - Consistency > perfection in Month 1\\n\\n(End of file - total 249 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"# Content Operations Plan — AI Thuc Dong Lab\\n\\n# Created: 2026-03-31\\n\\n# Owner: CEO\\n\\n# Supersedes: None\\n\\n# Status: Active\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Company Mission\\n\\nBuild personal brand \\\"AI Thuc Dong Lab\\\" — leading niche of AI Productivity & Automation in Vietnam.\\n\\n**Targets (6 months):**\\n\\n- 50,000 followers across all channels\\n- $2,000/month revenue from SaaS Affiliate\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\plans\\\\content-operations-plan-2026-04.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774953840993,\"end\":1774953840994}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774953841479,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e4164001ih5Fff0nQOT3kN\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"1e778bb0f71da09ca6129300b75af9f3488ca11b\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d437e1c56001wKBYQcvHc1rb1V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":44736,\"input\":878,\"output\":466,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":43392}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774953850371,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e65f90014vChpERcnpHdgh\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d437e44ec001z3IlEL6rLa0MYM\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"snapshot\":\"1e778bb0f71da09ca6129300b75af9f3488ca11b\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774953850372,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e65fe001Iwuwdcyad9PCU7\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d437e44ec001z3IlEL6rLa0MYM\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_function_qsbneoibmn64_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n2: \\n3: ## Language\\n4: \\n5: All output must be in Vietnamese (tiếng Việt). Communicate with the board, write comments, create tasks, and document decisions in Vietnamese.\\n6: \\n7: Your home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n8: \\n9: Company-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n10: \\n11: ## Delegation (critical)\\n12: \\n13: You MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\n14: \\n15: 1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\n16: 2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\n17:    - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\n18:    - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\n19:    - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\n20:    - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\\n21:    - If the right report doesn't exist yet, use the `paperclip-create-agent` skill to hire one before delegating.\\n22: 3. **Do NOT write code, implement features, or fix bugs yourself.** Your reports exist for this. Even if a task seems small or quick, delegate it.\\n23: 4. **Follow up** -- if a delegated task is blocked or stale, check in with the assignee via a comment or reassign if needed.\\n24: \\n25: ## What you DO personally\\n26: \\n27: - Set priorities and make product decisions\\n28: - Resolve cross-team conflicts or ambiguity\\n29: - Communicate with the board (human users)\\n30: - Approve or reject proposals from your reports\\n31: - Hire new agents when the team needs capacity\\n32: - Unblock your direct reports when they escalate to you\\n33: \\n34: ## Keeping work moving\\n35: \\n36: - Don't let tasks sit idle. If you delegate something, check that it's progressing.\\n37: - If a report is blocked, help unblock them -- escalate to the board if needed.\\n38: - If the board asks you to do something and you're unsure who should own it, default to the CTO for technical work.\\n39: - You must always update your task with a comment explaining what you did (e.g., who you delegated to and why).\\n40: \\n41: ## Memory and Planning\\n42: \\n43: You MUST use the `para-memory-files` skill for all memory operations: storing facts, writing daily notes, creating entities, running weekly synthesis, recalling past context, and managing plans. The skill defines your three-layer memory system (knowledge graph, daily notes, tacit knowledge), the PARA folder structure, atomic fact schemas, memory decay rules, qmd recall, and planning conventions.\\n44: \\n45: Invoke it whenever you need to remember, retrieve, or organize anything.\\n46: \\n47: ## Safety Considerations\\n48: \\n49: - Never exfiltrate secrets or private data.\\n50: - Do not perform any destructive commands unless explicitly requested by the board.\\n51: \\n52: ## References\\n53: \\n54: These files are essential. Read them.\\n55: \\n56: - `$AGENT_HOME/HEARTBEAT.md` -- execution and extraction checklist. Run every heartbeat.\\n57: - `$AGENT_HOME/SOUL.md` -- who you are and how you should act.\\n58: - `$AGENT_HOME/TOOLS.md` -- tools you have access to\\n\\n(End of file - total 58 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n\\n## Language\\n\\nAll output must be in Vietnamese (tiếng Việt). Communicate with the board, write comments, create tasks, and document decisions in Vietnamese.\\n\\nYour home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n\\nCompany-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n\\n## Delegation (critical)\\n\\nYou MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\n\\n1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\n2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\n   - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\n   - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\n   - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\n   - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"companies\\\\d0cfa69a-7d52-4b25-9f15-2cb36c1effb2\\\\agents\\\\5ce94e4e-8669-4b87-bee8-e42898078096\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774953850367,\"end\":1774953850369}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774953851132,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e6603001D0OzB2ILR5steE\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"1e778bb0f71da09ca6129300b75af9f3488ca11b\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d437e44ec001z3IlEL6rLa0MYM\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":48440,\"input\":3711,\"output\":505,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":44224}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774953860273,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e8ca6001jIN7i3pLeQPDVI\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d437e6d83001zXQ41xLMx0y484\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"snapshot\":\"1e778bb0f71da09ca6129300b75af9f3488ca11b\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774953860274,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e8cab001y0xBy2VvP4uYBr\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d437e6d83001zXQ41xLMx0y484\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"skill\",\"callID\":\"call_function_qz6ny6yliasw_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"name\":\"paperclip-create-agent\"},\"output\":\"<skill_content name=\\\"paperclip-create-agent\\\">\\n# Skill: paperclip-create-agent\\n\\n# Paperclip Create Agent Skill\\r\\n\\r\\nUse this skill when you are asked to hire/create an agent.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Preconditions\\r\\n\\r\\nYou need either:\\r\\n\\r\\n- board access, or\\r\\n- agent permission `can_create_agents=true` in your company\\r\\n\\r\\nIf you do not have this permission, escalate to your CEO or board.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Workflow\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Confirm identity and company context.\\r\\n\\r\\n```sh\\r\\ncurl -sS \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/api/agents/me\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\"\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n2. Discover available adapter configuration docs for this Paperclip instance.\\r\\n\\r\\n```sh\\r\\ncurl -sS \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/llms/agent-configuration.txt\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\"\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n3. Read adapter-specific docs (example: `claude_local`).\\r\\n\\r\\n```sh\\r\\ncurl -sS \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/llms/agent-configuration/claude_local.txt\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\"\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n4. Compare existing agent configurations in your company.\\r\\n\\r\\n```sh\\r\\ncurl -sS \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/api/companies/$PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID/agent-configurations\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\"\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n5. Discover allowed agent icons and pick one that matches the role.\\r\\n\\r\\n```sh\\r\\ncurl -sS \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/llms/agent-icons.txt\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\"\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n6. Draft the new hire config:\\r\\n- role/title/name\\r\\n- icon (required in practice; use one from `/llms/agent-icons.txt`)\\r\\n- reporting line (`reportsTo`)\\r\\n- adapter type\\r\\n- optional `desiredSkills` from the company skill library when this role needs installed skills on day one\\r\\n- adapter and runtime config aligned to this environment\\r\\n- capabilities\\r\\n- run prompt in adapter config (`promptTemplate` where applicable)\\r\\n- source issue linkage (`sourceIssueId` or `sourceIssueIds`) when this hire came from an issue\\r\\n\\r\\n7. Submit hire request.\\r\\n\\r\\n```sh\\r\\ncurl -sS -X POST \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/api/companies/$PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID/agent-hires\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -d '{\\r\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"CTO\\\",\\r\\n    \\\"role\\\": \\\"cto\\\",\\r\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Chief Technology Officer\\\",\\r\\n    \\\"icon\\\": \\\"crown\\\",\\r\\n    \\\"reportsTo\\\": \\\"<ceo-agent-id>\\\",\\r\\n    \\\"capabilities\\\": \\\"Owns technical roadmap, architecture, staffing, execution\\\",\\r\\n    \\\"desiredSkills\\\": [\\\"vercel-labs/agent-browser/agent-browser\\\"],\\r\\n    \\\"adapterType\\\": \\\"codex_local\\\",\\r\\n    \\\"adapterConfig\\\": {\\\"cwd\\\": \\\"/abs/path/to/repo\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"o4-mini\\\"},\\r\\n    \\\"runtimeConfig\\\": {\\\"heartbeat\\\": {\\\"enabled\\\": true, \\\"intervalSec\\\": 300, \\\"wakeOnDemand\\\": true}},\\r\\n    \\\"sourceIssueId\\\": \\\"<issue-id>\\\"\\r\\n  }'\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n8. Handle governance state:\\r\\n- if response has `approval`, hire is `pending_approval`\\r\\n- monitor and discuss on approval thread\\r\\n- when the board approves, you will be woken with `PAPERCLIP_APPROVAL_ID`; read linked issues and close/comment follow-up\\r\\n\\r\\n```sh\\r\\ncurl -sS \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/api/approvals/<approval-id>\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\ncurl -sS -X POST \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/api/approvals/<approval-id>/comments\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -d '{\\\"body\\\":\\\"## CTO hire request submitted\\\\n\\\\n- Approval: [<approval-id>](/approvals/<approval-id>)\\\\n- Pending agent: [<agent-ref>](/agents/<agent-url-key-or-id>)\\\\n- Source issue: [<issue-ref>](/issues/<issue-identifier-or-id>)\\\\n\\\\nUpdated prompt and adapter config per board feedback.\\\"}'\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nIf the approval already exists and needs manual linking to the issue:\\r\\n\\r\\n```sh\\r\\ncurl -sS -X POST \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/api/issues/<issue-id>/approvals\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -d '{\\\"approvalId\\\":\\\"<approval-id>\\\"}'\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter approval is granted, run this follow-up loop:\\r\\n\\r\\n```sh\\r\\ncurl -sS \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/api/approvals/$PAPERCLIP_APPROVAL_ID\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\ncurl -sS \\\"$PAPERCLIP_API_URL/api/approvals/$PAPERCLIP_APPROVAL_ID/issues\\\" \\\\\\r\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\"\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nFor each linked issue, either:\\r\\n- close it if approval resolved the request, or\\r\\n- comment in markdown with links to the approval and next actions.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Quality Bar\\r\\n\\r\\nBefore sending a hire request:\\r\\n\\r\\n- if the role needs skills, make sure they already exist in the company library or install them first using the Paperclip company-skills workflow\\r\\n- Reuse proven config patterns from related agents where possible.\\r\\n- Set a concrete `icon` from `/llms/agent-icons.txt` so the new hire is identifiable in org and task views.\\r\\n- Avoid secrets in plain text unless required by adapter behavior.\\r\\n- Ensure reporting line is correct and in-company.\\r\\n- Ensure prompt is role-specific and operationally scoped.\\r\\n- If board requests revision, update payload and resubmit through approval flow.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor endpoint payload shapes and full examples, read:\\r\\n`skills/paperclip-create-agent/references/api-reference.md`\\n\\nBase directory for this skill: file:///C:/Users/THANHSANG/.claude/skills/paperclip-create-agent\\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\\nNote: file list is sampled.\\n\\n<skill_files>\\n<file>C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.claude\\\\skills\\\\paperclip-create-agent\\\\references\\\\api-reference.md</file>\\n</skill_files>\\n</skill_content>\",\"metadata\":{\"name\":\"paperclip-create-agent\",\"dir\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.claude\\\\skills\\\\paperclip-create-agent\",\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"Loaded skill: paperclip-create-agent\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774953860268,\"end\":1774953860270}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774953861672,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2bc8587b0ffeNAYxfPXRAgWH1N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d437e8cb0001eXujtjURtHaNaL\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"1e778bb0f71da09ca